// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 3 „Minevik ja kogemused” (b1b2-011…015), stage B1+.
// Design v4 „task-based” (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_STATIONS.md §7, owner 2026-11-17) on the v3 station engine, built like the
// sample module 1 (b2/module01.js). Module goal (the learner): „Ma oskan oma minevikust selgelt ja huvitavalt jutustada”;
// module product „Minu lugu” (015 Kasuta: a card, then the S16 one-minute talk and the W1 letter to the library).
// The learner is the subject: his family's table, his experiences in Estonian nature, his own time line, a mistake he
// learned from. No storyline, no course cast. Every teaching lesson: exactly 4 stations (≤ 75 min) — hook + pre-task →
// input + task → language focus (notice → rule → use) → product in class (plan + first sentences) + „Kui aega jääb”
// extension + exit check + „Ma oskan …”; the long writing and a 1-minute voice message are homework; the lesson's words
// reach „Harjuta” through vocabulary/lessonWords/b1b2.json (Sõnavara → Teemad).
// One format and one everyday topic a lesson, no two neighbours alike (admin/course/v4Tasks.test.js):
//   011 game    „Mis oli sinu lapsepõlve pühadelaual?”           family   final present: a family food story (W05)
//   012 infogap „Kas sa oled kunagi rabas käinud?”               nature   final negotiate: call the hike leader (S05)
//   013 case    „Teletorn, 21. august 1991: mis oli juhtunud enne?” culture  final explain: tell a child why 20 August (W12)
//   014 project „Viga, millest ma õppisin”                        money    final advise: a warning story told in 2 min (S16)
//   015 exam    Kontroll 3 in Harno B2 form + „Minu lugu” as the S16 one-minute talk.
// Grammar (roadmap: every past tied to its function, by discovery and spiralled): 011 lihtminevik = an event (strong
// verbs, negation ei + -nud), 012 täisminevik = an experience vs lihtminevik = a dated event, 013 enneminevik = what had
// happened before (enne kui, pärast seda kui, selleks ajaks), 014 the three pasts together in a story + the past
// conditional of regret (oleksin pidanud). The module's Harno topic „toit” (academicTopics.js) lives in the topic opener
// (011 station 2, after a 12-minute hook and game) and in 015; the module's one long text is that opener.
// Pronunciation: 012 station 1 (short past forms, one sound apart), 013 station 3 (first-syllable stress, teacher note).
// Input across the module: the topic page (011), audio (011 model story, 012 radio, 013 history minute, 014 scam call),
// case cards (013), a chart (014). Exam corners (finalShape V12): 011 R2b, 012 L3, 013 L1, 014 S1.
import { B, tag, teach, withShapes } from '../blocks.js';
import { exitCheck, extension, homeTask, purpose, station } from '../stationBlocks.js';

// a talk with the teacher as the partner, done in the lesson (engine/inLesson.js), not a home recording
const inLesson = (block) => ({ ...block, inLesson: true });
// the lesson's grammar as the small subtitle under the title on every sheet
const grammar = (text) => ({
  discover: { label: '1 Avasta', slot: 1, subtitle: text },
  practice: { label: '2 Harjuta', slot: 2, subtitle: text },
  transfer: { label: '3 Kasuta', slot: 3, subtitle: text },
});
// the home task card at the end of every lesson
const homework = (id, items) => B.phrasebank(id, [['Kodutöö', items]]);
const WORDS_HOME = 'Tunni sõnad: Sõnavara → Teemad → Moodul 3. Kui teema on läbitud, kordad sõnu „Harjuta” all.';
// a learner who cannot record (no quiet room, no smartphone) says the talk at the start of the next lesson
const NO_RECORDING = 'Kui salvestada ei saa, räägi see järgmise tunni alguses õpetajale.';

// an exam part header carries the goal of its part: b2/lessonGoals.test.js asks every non-text block of a B2 sheet for one
// of the lesson's goals, and the header has none of its own (B.examPart: goal '')
const PART = (id, skill, o) => ({ ...B.examPart(id, skill, o), goal: ['R', 'L'].includes(skill) ? 'g_read' : 'g_use' });

